course: dictionary
lesson: 7518
title: Power: many meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Power is one word with several meanings, so context tells you which one is meant. Read the words around it and ask: what is the power doing here? «In 1986 a reactor at the Chornobyl power plant exploded and spread radiation.» Here power means electricity, the energy that runs machines.
explain: «A cliché is a phrase used so often that it has lost its power.» Here power means strength: the phrase no longer has the force to make people feel or notice anything. Try the swap: "has lost its strength" fits the sentence, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Power can also be a verb, a doing word. «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills» means the stems are burned to give the mills energy so they can work. When you see power with a word like "to" or "the" before it, check whether it is a doing word.
fact: Power is the ability or strength to do something or to make things happen.
fact: Power can mean control over people, as in «the Bolsheviks, who had taken power in Russia».
fact: Power can mean energy, especially electricity, as in «a power cut» or «a power station».
fact: To power something means to give it energy so it works.
fact: In maths, a power is how many times a number is multiplied by itself: 2 to the power of 3 is 2 × 2 × 2 = 8.
exercise: «In 1986 a reactor at the Chornobyl power plant exploded and spread radiation.» In this sentence, what does power mean? | *Electricity, the energy that runs machines | A kind of magic | A strong push or shove | Being in charge of a country
exercise: «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» Here power is a doing word. What does to power mean? | To make something very small | To win a fight | *To give energy so a machine works | To stop something moving
exercise: Maths: In 2 to the power of 3, what is the answer? | 6 | 5 | *8 | 9
test: «Bolsheviks, who had taken power in Russia.» What does power mean here? | *Control over a country | Strength in a muscle | A special superhero ability | Electricity for lights
test: «A cliché is a phrase used so often that it has lost its power.» What does power mean here? | Its energy source | Its number of letters | Its ability to fly | *Its strength to affect people
exam: Which sentence uses power to mean energy, not control or strength? | «Christians believe God's power is beyond the ordinary.» | «Sam used all his power to lift the box.» | *«A power cut left the whole street in the dark.» | «The king had great power over his people.»
